@startuml
title FST-050 - Consented loopback proxy and website decisions
autonumber
actor Learner
participant Browser
participant "Owned network settings\n+ recovery guardian" as Settings
participant "Loopback PAC / HTTP proxy" as Proxy
participant "Session + consent + policy" as Current
participant "Transactional event outbox" as Events
participant "Requested origin" as Origin
participant "Local feedback" as UI
Learner -> Settings : explicit forwarding / temporary settings consent
alt system proxy routing
  Settings -> Settings : snapshot originals + persist ownership journal
  Settings -> Browser : configure supported routing
else explicit Linux Brave routing
  Learner -> Settings : request existing-profile Brave setup
  Settings --> Learner : close Brave within 60 seconds (no forced exit)
  Learner -> Browser : close all Brave windows, including dev UI
  Settings -> Browser : launch native Brave with PAC + verification address
end
Browser -> Proxy : verify local routing challenge
note over Browser, Proxy
  Report unverified browsers / permissions explicitly.
  PAC routes traffic; policy stays in the proxy to avoid PAC cache delays.
end note
Browser -> Proxy : HTTP request or HTTPS CONNECT(host:port)
Proxy -> Proxy : validate authority, framing and resource bounds
Proxy -> Current : read committed consent, running unexpired WORK, rule
Current --> Proxy : most-specific enabled domain decision or none
alt eligible matching rule
  Proxy -> Events : commit DistractionDetected (host only)
  alt BLOCK
    Proxy -> Current : recheck eligibility and selected rule
    alt still selected
      Proxy --> Browser : reject request; no upstream connection
      Proxy -> Events : commit correlated DistractionBlocked
      Proxy -> UI : blocked website feedback
    else stale decision
      Proxy -> Proxy : reevaluate before forwarding
    end
  else LOG or WARN
    opt WARN
      Proxy -> UI : local warning
    end
    Proxy -> Origin : forward client-requested bytes
    Origin --> Browser : response through proxy
  end
else no blocking decision / paused / break / stopped
  Proxy -> Origin : forward client-requested bytes
  Origin --> Browser : response through proxy
end
note over Proxy, Origin
  HTTPS CONNECT tunnels preserve encrypted TLS bytes.
  No certificates, TLS interception, telemetry or payload persistence.
end note
loop session / policy reconciliation
  Proxy -> Current : recheck existing tunnel hosts
  Proxy -> Proxy : close only newly BLOCK-selected tunnels
end
Learner -> Settings : disable / stop application
Settings -> Settings : compare-and-restore owned originals
Settings -> Proxy : close after restoration
note over Settings, Proxy
  Independent lease restores settings after disconnect.
  Restart recovers journals; concurrent user changes are preserved.
  Native browser/OS verification is required before claiming support.
end note
@enduml
